openthread-br: fix the build with GCC 14

Not ours. Copied unmodified from openwrt/packages, where it is
net/openthread-br/patches/100-fix-gcc14-build.patch and has been since
2025-05-25. Renumbered here to fit this feed's ordering; the diff is
byte-identical to the original.

Author: Tianling Shen <cnsztl@immortalwrt.org>
Origin: https://github.com/openwrt/packages/commit/937e2a5b809cbd21bee7bf8d1e7c2bb90ad21275

The mbedtls copy vendored inside the openthread submodule guards a
byte-by-byte tail case on the compiler; GCC 14.1 and later need the same
guard the IAR compiler already had, or the build fails.

--- a/third_party/openthread/repo/third_party/mbedtls/repo/library/common.h
+++ b/third_party/openthread/repo/third_party/mbedtls/repo/library/common.h
@@ -199,7 +199,7 @@ static inline void mbedtls_xor(unsigned
         uint8x16_t x = veorq_u8(v1, v2);
         vst1q_u8(r + i, x);
     }
-#if defined(__IAR_SYSTEMS_ICC__)
+#if defined(__IAR_SYSTEMS_ICC__) || (defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC) && MBEDTLS_GCC_VERSION >= 140100)
     /* This if statement helps some compilers (e.g., IAR) optimise out the byte-by-byte tail case
      * where n is a constant multiple of 16.
      * For other compilers (e.g. recent gcc and clang) it makes no difference if n is a compile-time
